669B OBS scripts (Node Playwright library, not the MCP). Node 20 (nvm); Playwright resolves from the worktree's frontend/node_modules or the sibling main checkout's. lib.cjs is 669A's lib.cjs with the raw dir renamed (/tmp/669B-$PHASE-raw/), the login wait widened to /platform-admin, and two additions (PA base URL, mailpitOtp() — Mailpit's read-only REST); it re-uses ../../../661B/walk/scripts/common.cjs (theme, sidebar cookie, console watch, sheet()).
  00-seed.cjs       RUN ONCE (done for before; idempotent — a re-run only appends a run entry to seed.json runs[]). Read-only inventory; probes + shoots the naturally empty /platform-admin/access-requests (4 tabs × 1024/1440 light) BEFORE any write; then the writes, all through the browser: two access requests via the public /request-access form (OTP read from Mailpit REST), and Reject of the second via the Reject dialog. NEVER Approves. Writes ../seed.json.
  01-capture.cjs    capture: 12 targets × alice/bob/carol (45 page loads; /org/ pages 1024/1440 × light/dark, platform-admin light only) + team interactions (row click → MemberDetailPanel, row hover colours, keyboard Tab → Enter) for Alice 1440 light / 1024 dark and Carol 1440 light / 1024 dark. Read-only: tabs clicked, a search typed, two Sheets opened and Escaped. Raw → /tmp/669B-$PHASE-raw/.
  03-sel-compat.sh  SEL-COMPAT suites, specs unchanged: pnpm test:e2e:navigation + pnpm test:e2e e2e/tests/auth/rbac-capabilities.spec.ts (E2E_AUTH_MODE=mock, PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001) → $RAW/suites.json; restores frontend/test-results + documentation/screenshots.
  02-assemble.cjs   JSON (measurements / sel-compat incl. suites / console / discover) + 9 contact sheets + 3 defect crops → ../../$PHASE/.
  probe.cjs         the in-page probe (structure-agnostic: raw tables / hand-rolled headers and DataTable / PageHeader alike; platform-admin scope = <body> while it has no #main-content).
Order used for before: 00-seed → 01-capture → 03-sel-compat.sh → 01-capture (re-run after adding the row-hover interaction; read-only) → 02-assemble.
OBS-after (same data, frontend rebuilt from the slice head; do NOT re-seed), from this directory, unedited:
  PHASE=after node 01-capture.cjs && PHASE=after bash 03-sel-compat.sh && PHASE=after STACK="<frontend image + SHA>" node 02-assemble.cjs
